
## Training

- `make check` trains for two steps on the CPU; keep it that fast. Real runs
  go through `make train`, and on a rented
  GPU through `hi compute` (see the hi skill).
- Every run writes its config next to its results in `results/`; never
  change a config without changing where its results go.
- PyTorch comes from one dependency group per machine, which `make` picks:
  `cpu`, `cuda`, or `rocm` (Strix Halo). Run Python through `make` targets;
  a plain `uv run` reinstalls the CPU build. Never add `torch` to the
  project's main dependencies.
